      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T22:46:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why not add another parameter here: reboot_requested and then reboot in the end of this function, once tpm resest (and possibly wipe out) are completed).\n\n\nas suggested the meaning of the first parameter changes, but there are other users of this function which would want to wipe out the tpm but not to reboot the device.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 657,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b35f9c6_a5bef7a9",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 657,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:35:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function looks like it can be called from any context. My concern is that we lock things  accordingly. We\u0027re clobbering lots of globals from any number contexts that could be pre-empted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 657,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d285ffbc_bc1abdf3",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 657,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T02:13:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there is already a reset in progress we don\u0027t proceed until it is complete. So we can\u0027t clobber the globals.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 657,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d04852db_5ab47208",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 657,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T04:38:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See my comment below about how we\u0027re basically blocking all requests at that point. Additionally, we\u0027re just making the request -- not actually resetting. By returning EC_ERROR_BUSY we are dropping important requests on the floor.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 657,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8fe71a2_dd802632",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 657,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T17:51:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"This function looks like it can be called from any context. \"\n\nThis is a good point. How about we introduce another function, just to send an event to the tpm task, and then have the tpm task call this function which can do everything what\u0027s required.\n\nSo, there would be two reset options:\n- reboot\n- wipe nvmem\n\nthey could be communicated though different event types sent  to the tpm task to avoid the need for global variables.  A mechanism is still needed to provide both asyn and sync implementations.",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24646153_998f465b",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 657,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T17:57:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need another function. This is that function. Naming it to express the semantics a \u0027request\u0027 is important. After that we just need to ensure we handle the different contexts being able to call this function. Global variables are fine. Just disable interrupts and set the variables you want. Then re-enable interrupts. When the task processes them in tpm_reset_now() it disables interrupts, snapshots the state, clears it, then re-enables interrupts. After that it takes action on the request provided the request state.",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "572fc2d8_b0cb745e",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 669,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:35:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So we can\u0027t accumulate wipes or reboots if a reset is already pending. That breaks the semantics of a lot of the callers. This function is about requesting action. I think we should honor the requests as best we can. Or at least document how we can drop requests on the floor (which I think is a bad idea).",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92299e35_f24615fa",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:35:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tpm_reset_now() shouldn\u0027t take any parameters. The function can pull the requests from the state it\u0027s keeping. I suggest we put the information into a struct such that it\u0027s easy to reason about the globals that would be set during a reboot request.\n\nThis call here can be replaced with this:\n\ntpm_request_reset().",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68f13157_89c4d4c1",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T17:51:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this function would be combined with tpm_reset() above if the suggestion to do everything on the tpm task context triggered by an event  is accepted.",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d64e5bfd_cb4bcab7",
        "filename": "common/tpm_registers.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T17:57:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The tpm task can send a request to itself. My point is that once you have the request semantics in place this call doesn\u0027t need to be different from the other callers. Within the while loop we\u0027ll see and process the request.",
      "revId": "8c9ba3b855aed1da9b87faf93cf1ef52ae84634c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
